MID_LGV_1_M08_Kai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Kai_m01_001: I know everyone has a wish they want to fulfill too,\nbut someone has to lose.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Kai_m01_002: I wish everybody in the games could get whatever\nthey want or need.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Kai_m01_003: But I suppose that's not how the world works, huh?
MID_LGA_1_M08_Kai_m01: <BLN>Someone has to lose...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Bel_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Bel_m01_001: I am a prisoner and a gladiator, which means I have\nbeen forced to endure every injustice.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Bel_m01_002: Yet I sensed no selfishness from the Divine\nSovereign when he offered to have me compete.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Bel_m01_003: A pawn I may be in his game, but I do believe he\nrespected my wishes.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Bel_m01_004: Not that a mere gladiator can divine the intentions of\na god...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Bel_m01_005: <NCA>Tell him the Divine Sovereign meant well.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Bel_m01_006: <NCB>Tell him he did it on a whim.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Bel_m01_007: <ACA>You feel as I do. It seems he is principled in his way.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Bel_m01_008: <ACB>Yes, you might be right. Certainly that was my\nsuspicion—and perhaps there's no more to it.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Bel_m01: <BLN>What say you?
MID_LGV_1_M08_Dit_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Dit_m01_001: If only I didn't have to traverse the sea to reach an\narena like this one.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Dit_m01_002: I would be able to abandon myself to battle, day\nafter day... It would be glorious. And yet...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Dit_m01_003: Were that the case, I would never have entered these\ngames. So I suppose it is to the good that there is not.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Dit_m01: <BLN>If only Fódlan had an arena...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Tal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Tal_m01_001: The collection of poetry Fianna picked out for me\nwas pretty good. She has great taste.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Tal_m01_002: She's got the heart of a poet herself. It's no wonder\nthat she knows her stuff.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Tal_m01_003: I asked if I could see any of her own poetry, but\nshe got shy and locked herself in her room...
MID_LGA_1_M08_Tal_m01: <BLN>Fianna is a poet.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Orh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Orh_m01_001: Though I'm here for the Heroic Games, I still take\nmy duties as a lead priest seriously.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Orh_m01_002: I've lived my life in service to Credna and all of\nthose who believe in him with all their hearts.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Orh_m01_003: Credna would probably tell me to go a bit easier\non myself. Still, I'll always be committed!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Orh_m01: <BLN>My duties come first!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Seo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Seo_m01_001: The land of Dagda is vast. It takes a long time to\ntravel from Megaira, the capital of Saramis, to here.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Seo_m01_002: But legend has it that the land was vaster still once—\nthat the sea between Saramis and Mosa did not exist.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Seo_m01_003: Bonaventure suspects the sea is a product of the era\nof the gods, but I suppose only the gods would know.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Seo_m01: <BLN>The land of Dagda is vast.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Led_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Led_m01_001: So, the Divine Sovereign will grant a wish.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Led_m01_002: Humans have any number of wishes they can't fulfill\non their own, so what better reward could there be?
MID_LGV_1_M08_Led_m01_003: I'm not sure if it's a kindness or a cruelty that he's\nmaking us fight to determine whose gets granted.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Led_m01: <BLN>One wish, huh?
MID_LGV_1_M08_Anh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Anh_m01_001: Dagsion is vast. So many people and places, all so\nclose together. I'm still not entirely adapted to it.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Anh_m01_002: Master Long tried to encourage me. He said most\nwho leave the village end up feeling this way.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Anh_m01_003: Sha Lan has made the same journey as me, but she's\nadapted quickly. So why can't I?
MID_LGA_1_M08_Anh_m01: <BLN>Why can't I?
MID_LGV_1_M08_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Tia_m01_001: I'm so lucky I found a book as thick as this! I'm going\nto be reading this one for quite some time. Hehe.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Tia_m01_002: It was kind of expensive, but I think the substantial\namount of content reflects the price.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Tia_m01_003: I'll have to be careful to not get carried away staying\nup all night reading!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Tia_m01: <BLN>I'm so lucky!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Pet_m01_001: Books are really expensive, aren't they? I don't\nread, so I'd never realized it before.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Pet_m01_002: Tialla goes from one book to the next, always reading\nsomething new. She's really impressive.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Pet_m01_003: But, I mean, just supposing I married Tialla? Paying\nfor all those books would be rough, wouldn't it?
MID_LGV_1_M08_Pet_m01_004: <NCA>Tell him she'd be earning too.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Pet_m01_005: <NCB>Warn him he'll have to spend less on food.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Pet_m01_006: <ACA>True! I spend as much on food as she does on books,\nso I guess we're similar that way.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Pet_m01_007: <ACB>Urgh, yeah, maybe. It'd be tough, but I'd do it for her.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Pet_m01: <BLN>Tialla's so impressive...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Hur_m01_001: Peppe caused trouble in the marketplace. Again.\nI've got to give him a proper talking-to later.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Hur_m01_002: He was shouting, "Delicious fish! I'll buy the lot!"\nWhich is something no kid can do.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Hur_m01_003: The merchant said they looked forward to him doing\nthat once he becomes king, which really set him off.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Hur_m01: <BLN>I'll give him a talking-to...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Max_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Max_m01_001: The main matches of the Heroic Games are bound to\nbe quite the event! Ooh, I can't wait.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Max_m01_002: Plus, I heard that a certain demon's going to\ntake part.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Max_m01_003: Heh heh HEH! Gotta sharpen my blade. Make it nice\nand shiny for the big show!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Max_m01: <BLN>Gotta sharpen my blade.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Gol_m01_001: I've been a gladiator awhile, but I've never seen the\nReaper in person.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Gol_m01_002: When he was fighting that guy, my big brother had\nthis weird look on his face...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Gol_m01_003: It's making me REALLY worry about him. You think\nsome grilled meat would cheer him up?
MID_LGA_1_M08_Gol_m01: <BLN>Been doing this a long time.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Gat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Gat_m01_001: There's no shortage of rumors about Drake's\ntreasures.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Gat_m01_002: Among them, that those who have them are drawn\nto one another, and are bound to meet.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Gat_m01_003: The powers of the warriors in the main matches\nsuggest that... That caution would be advised.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Gat_m01: <BLN>Be wary of the treasures.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Dan_m01_001: In cities and festivals, people gather and interact—\nand from those collisions are stories born!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Dan_m01_002: That's why I suggest attending branch temple\nfestivals in the capital, even if you're not devout.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Dan_m01: <BLN>Worth the trip!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Fab_m01_001: Black-Lace Ninae... I hear she is a vulkan who can\ncomprehend the words of spirits.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Fab_m01_002: Yet the rumors that she is poor at conversing with\nthe other beasts are true, it seems.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Fab_m01_003: How else do you explain the fact that she has not\ndivulged the nature of the spirits and spirit magic?
MID_LGV_1_M08_Fab_m01_004: I am glad of it, but I do sympathize. My own values\nare no better understood.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Fab_m01: <BLN>Black-Lace Ninae...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Esm_m01_001: There's an archery stall in the city. I landed an arrow\nsmack in the center of the target!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Esm_m01_002: Dad made sure I could shoot, just in case the time\ncame when we couldn't fish.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Esm_m01_003: I wonder if he'd be happy to see me win a prize. Too\nbad I can't show him.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Esm_m01: <BLN>I wish I could show my dad.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Urs_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Urs_m01_001: Fighting in the arena makes me feel like a beast\nin some freak show... A spectacle to be gawked at.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Urs_m01_002: ...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Urs_m01_003: If Talimun weren't here, I would never participate in\n"games" like this.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Urs_m01: <BLN>I don't like it...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Sim_m01_001: People who are good at business... What do they\nthink about all day, numbers?
MID_LGV_1_M08_Sim_m01_002: The only thing I wager in negotiations is my own\nlife. Not sure I have anything else to offer.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Sim_m01: <BLN>I don't get it...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lou_m01_001: Father, do you see me? Your little Lulu is growing up\nand absolutely crushing the Heroic Games!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lou_m01_002: I hope you're watching...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lou_m01_003: But I know you're busy. As a souvenir, I'll bring you\na splendid victory!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Lou_m01: <BLN>Watch me, Dad!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Fia_m01_001: When bad things happen, tea always has a way of\nsoothing the spirit.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Fia_m01_002: I just... I wish I had time to actually brew more tea.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Fia_m01_003: I need to learn to be strong without it... Yes, just\nlike Talimun.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Fia_m01: <BLN>I want to be strong...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Die_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Die_m01_001: I'm low on medicinal herbs. I should head into\nthe forest to stock up.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Die_m01_002: Priests insist on using sacred magic for all ills,\nbut sometimes medicine works better.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Die_m01_003: Besides, forest gathering is a Har Hali tradition.\nIt's part of who I am.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Die_m01: <BLN>I'm low on herbs.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lor_m01_001: Something...scary happened.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lor_m01_002: I was snacking on berries...when suddenly there\nwere way more in the bag.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lor_m01_003: Was that a berry ghost or something?!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lor_m01_004: <NCA>Tell her it wasn't.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lor_m01_005: <NCB>Agree with her.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lor_m01_006: <ACA>Huh? Well, you might be right. The new ones are\nall my favorites.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lor_m01_007: <ACA>How could a ghost figure that out about me?\nHey! It had to be the priest lady. Thanks!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lor_m01_008: <ACB>Nooo! Why'd you say that! Now I won't be able to\nget to sleep tonight!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Lor_m01: <BLN>Guess what...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Set_m01_001: I'm somewhat of a weapons aficionado, but I\nactually don't like battles at all.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Set_m01_002: I dislike them to the extreme. I believe that power is\nmeant to protect others, not harm them.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Set_m01_003: Enemies should cross blades only as a last resort.\nA clash of words can lead to resolution.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Set_m01: <BLN>I dislike violence.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Nin_m01_001: Long before the Heroic Games, another competition\nwas held in the arena.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Nin_m01_002: A warrior selected by Solel and another chosen by\nMars faced off in the Duel for the Gods.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Nin_m01_003: I remember it all—the magic axe, the Smoldering\nSword, the clash of battle ringing out.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Nin_m01: <BLN>Long ago...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Bon_m01_001: According to legend, there was once a great\ncivilization in this land called Iskandariya.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Bon_m01_002: They worshipped a god even older than the Dagdan\npantheon and knew the unique art of shaping life.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Bon_m01_003: However, they were destroyed by Dagda the\nGreat as he seized power. It is a sadly familiar tale.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Bon_m01: <BLN>It is a sadly familiar tale.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Tob_m01_001: Perfect. It's a great feeling when you can get your\nhair looking just right.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Tob_m01_002: I wear mine in a warrior's style, shaped with hair oil\nnative to Saramis.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Tob_m01_003: Now that I got my hair right, I'm ready to give it all\nI got in battle today! Baw haw haw!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Tob_m01: <BLN>Gonna give it my all!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lil_m01_001: We've finally hit the main matches for the Heroic\nGames. It's been a while since our last bout, huh?
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lil_m01_002: Without matches to fight in, I don't have as much\nwork to do, so I earn less.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lil_m01_003: But we'll probably be fighting tougher opponents\nfrom now on, so maybe I could ask for more.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Lil_m01: <BLN>I should renegotiate my fee.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lys_m01_001: The last time Commander Tobias was drunk, he\noffered me hair oil so I could style my hair like his.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lys_m01_002: I have my doubts it would suit me. I'm reluctant\nto even try.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lys_m01_003: <NCA>Agree that it's best as is.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lys_m01_004: <NCB>Suggest trying it out.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lys_m01_005: <ACA>I agree completely. Luckily, Commander Tobias has\nalmost certainly forgotten the suggestion by now.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lys_m01_006: <ACB>Have you taken leave of your senses? If that was\na joke, it wasn't a very good one.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Lys_m01: <BLN>How should I respond?
MID_LGV_1_M08_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Buc_m01_001: My resolve never wavers. I will meet the next match\nwith solemn strength.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Buc_m01_002: Whether it be for Lord Guillermo or milady, I will do\nas I must.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Buc_m01: <BLN>Lord Guillermo...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Sci_m01_001: Travel attire suits me far better than a full suit\nof armor.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Sci_m01_002: Were I overtly armed, I might intimidate others.\nCertainly I'd scare off women.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Sci_m01_003: Dressing light allows me to blend in wherever I am,\nwhich is all the better for my work.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Sci_m01: <BLN>I've tried it before.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Moo_m01_001: The marketplace here always has so many rare\ningredients and medicinal herbs for sale.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Moo_m01_002: I bet I can use them to come up with another new\nrecipe. It's gonna be great!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Moo_m01: <BLN>I'll make something new!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Mic_m01_001: Do you think the gods' parent-child relationships ever\nrun aground? They must, right?
MID_LGV_1_M08_Mic_m01_002: I'd love to ask them how they manage to make up\nand hold things together.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Mic_m01: <BLN>I'd love to ask them.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Oly_m01_001: Finally, the main matches of the Heroic Games have\nbegun...and I can't help but feel on edge.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Oly_m01_002: Those who have made it this far are flourishing\nblossoms, with no petals lost.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Oly_m01_003: Yet as violent as this performance may be, it shall be\nno less beautiful.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Oly_m01: <BLN>Finally, the main matches!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Naz_m01_001: Maybe it's the Heroic Games that's brought them to\ntown, but there's some bad folks walking around.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Naz_m01_002: The times they've tried to cause trouble, I've easily\nsent them packing.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Naz_m01_003: I'm small, but my muscles are stronger than a regular\nhuman's are!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Naz_m01_004: My combat skills are superior too. Those guys don't\nstand a chance against me!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Naz_m01: <BLN>They don't stand a chance!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Sar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Sar_m01_001: The White-Maned Demon won. But the Reaper...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Sar_m01_002: He's the one who truly worries me.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Sar_m01: <BLN>The one I'm worried about.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Dai_m01_001: I heard you can earn reward money if ya catch\nsomeone doing something bad in the city.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Dai_m01_002: But Anatolia really laid into me when I punched a\nbad-looking guy as soon as I saw him.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Dai_m01_003: I just thought if we had money, we could eat and she\nwouldn't have to work so much.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Dai_m01_004: <NCA>Scold him for punching.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Dai_m01_005: <NCB>Tell him to wait for a crime first.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Dai_m01_006: <ACA>Anatolia's strong, but she can do fortune-telling.\nMy strength is all I've got to offer!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Dai_m01_007: <ACB>That's kinda tedious, ain't it? Not my style.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Dai_m01: <BLN>I just want to help!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Hal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Hal_m01_001: Sometimes people think the sleight of hand I perform\nfor them is actually real magic. 
MID_LGV_1_M08_Hal_m01_002: Some of them call me a cheat or a fraud. Others ask\na thousand questions. Urgh.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Hal_m01_003: Maybe I'm doing the tricks so well that it fools them?\nI'm gonna let that make me feel extra confident!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Hal_m01: <BLN>Maybe I fooled them too well?
MID_LGV_1_M08_Guj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Guj_m01_001: There are lots of wealthy people in the capital, so\nit's fairly easy to earn money.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Guj_m01_002: On the other hand, I find that a tavern can stick you\nwith a strangely high bill too. Sobering, really.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Guj_m01_003: So my advice is to balance your profits with the\nbest taverns to socialize in!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Guj_m01: <BLN>A good time is possible!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Yan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Yan_m01_001: Fragrant aromas! Profound flavors! Truly, tipple is a\nbalm for this world's constant wobbliness!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Yan_m01_002: In the land of Sai, some even call it a curative.\nIt's a better balm than kneeling for gods anyway.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Yan_m01: <BLN>Tipple, not kneeling!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Iio_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Iio_m01_001: Long ago, I liked reading chronicles of heroism, but\nI'm not so fond of them now.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Iio_m01_002: Such reading makes the chasm between me as I\nam and my ideal of myself far too troubling.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Iio_m01_003: But I recently reread the tale my mother gave me\nlong ago—an epic one about Aragonian knights.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Iio_m01_004: Ah, in it, a band of knights serve a good king, live\nloyally, and fight nobly for their nation and people.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Iio_m01: <BLN>Heroic tales...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Pep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Pep_m01_001: The Heroic Games are superb, and we have met\nspectators whom we've cheered along with!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Pep_m01_002: We find the highs and lows of watching the games\nfascinating. We now "get" fanatical enthusiasm!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Pep_m01_003: We drew some laughs because we were watching\nthe audience and not the event.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Pep_m01_004: We hope that we are understanding it all. In any\ncase, there's always spectacle on and off the field!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Pep_m01: <BLN>Endlessly interesting!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Noc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Noc_m01_001: The final contestants have been decided. I can't\nwait for more. Those still in the games are so strong!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Noc_m01_002: It doesn't matter to me who wins. I just want to see\nmatches like this!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Noc_m01: <BLN>It's so exciting!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Sop_m01_001: I thought Anna's work would ease once the\nqualifiers were done, but that hasn't been the case.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Sop_m01_002: I know she takes games coordination seriously, but\nis that all she's doing? She looks SO exhausted!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Sop_m01_003: I wonder if there's anything I can do to help her.\nHmm, I'm not bad with shoulder massages.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Sop_m01: <BLN>Poor Anna...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Cat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Cat_m01_001: I caught Leda's performance at the tavern. I was\nenthralled. What flair and power!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Cat_m01_002: She's a sterling musician, though it's curious how\nthere's a...steel edge under all her passion.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Cat_m01_003: Though I consider my eyes and ears keen, I\ncouldn't quite find the reason for it.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Cat_m01_004: Oh, it's you, Leda! You could have interrupted me\nat any time there, you know!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Cat_m01: <BLN>Sterling all around, but...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Ned_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Ned_m01_001: The orniuses have such different looks and\ncharacters—the meganiuses too. It's so interesting!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Ned_m01_002: I once served as an ornius rider in Saramis. I prefer\nan ornius with a rougher temperament.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Ned_m01_003: Of course, then the warrior astride the animal\nneeds to have a valiant disposition.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Ned_m01: <BLN>They look the same, but...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Zac_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Zac_m01_001: Those guys livin' it up had plates piled with meat.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Zac_m01_002: Bunch of scum, not gettin' how vegetables are the\nmovers and shakers in a good dish.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Zac_m01: <BLN>They don't get it!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Maj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Maj_m01_001: I hate lines! People should get outta the way\nwhen the great Majide's around!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Maj_m01_002: But when I shove ahead, the temple guards\ncome at me. The world ain't right!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Maj_m01: <BLN>The world ain't right!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Ven_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Ven_m01_001: Why won't anyone pay heed to my battle\nstrategies? People just scatter when I expound!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Ven_m01_002: Lamentable—throwing away a rare chance to learn\nfrom me, THE General Benditz!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Ven_m01_003: I pay proper attention to those who share their\ntactical thoughts with me, of course.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Ven_m01: <BLN>Lamentable!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Ini_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Ini_m01_001: These other mercenaries are amazing. How do\nthey negotiate their pay so skillfully?
MID_LGV_1_M08_Ini_m01_002: Even if I earn myself a pay raise, I find it so hard\nto actually ask for one.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Ini_m01_003: Just thinking of doing that makes me tense up!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Ini_m01: <BLN>Amazing, all of them.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Jas_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Jas_m01_001: Seeing couples being happy reminds me of the\ndays when my fellow was still alive...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Jas_m01_002: Nice to stop thinking about raising funds for a bit\nand take a walk down memory lane like that.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Jas_m01: <BLN>The old days...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Ale_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Ale_m01_001: Will I ever meet the one I'm truly destined to\nbe with?
MID_LGV_1_M08_Ale_m01_002: Someone who I'd share a real love with—not\nchosen for me by someone else?
MID_LGA_1_M08_Ale_m01: <BLN>Will it ever happen?
MID_LGV_1_M08_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Cen_m01_001: Occasionally we see some spectators get too excited\nand start brawling in the arena.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Cen_m01_002: During the main matches, the crowd's enthusiasm is\nbeyond measure, so we keep an eye out for trouble.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Cen_m01_003: It's regrettable, though, that those of us who serve\nthe temples have no time to enjoy spectating.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Cen_m01: <BLN>We have to keep an eye out...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Kir_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Kir_m01_001: I've got to get my hands on a lot of money. Now!\nAll at once! Not scrounging for it, little by little.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Kir_m01_002: Stealing from people is easy enough, but I've got\nto be careful not to make waves.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Kir_m01_003: Ahhh... I miss the easy life of a pirate.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Kir_m01: <BLN>I miss easy money...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Nuz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Nuz_m01_001: The city is foreign to me. But the way the buildings\noverlap is like a forest, in a way.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Nuz_m01_002: Though I'm told that running across roofs as one\nmight leap between trees is not allowed.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Nuz_m01_003: The temple soldiers scolded me for it. I have learned\nmy lesson...to not get caught.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Nuz_m01: <BLN>The city is foreign to me.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Gab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Gab_m01_001: I got a real bargain on some weapons for the\nRenewal Ceremony!
MID_LGV_1_M08_Gab_m01_002: A little worse for wear, sure, but they'll probably\nlast through the match.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Gab_m01_003: And then I clean 'em up a little, find someone who's\nin the market... Hehehehe.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Gab_m01: <BLN>You can still use 'em.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lin_m01_001: Sometimes the image of my mother comes to\nmind unbidden.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Lin_m01_002: I will return to her someday. I refuse to rot away\nuntil that happens.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Lin_m01: <BLN>One day...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Nat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Nat_m01_001: The White-Maned Demon... There can't be any\ndoubt now. That is General Bertrand.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Nat_m01_002: I'd heard he was executed. So how is this possible?
MID_LGA_1_M08_Nat_m01: <BLN>The White-Maned Demon.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Hri_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Hri_m01_001: It seems I earned the ire of that, ah, heretofore\nmasked priest.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Hri_m01_002: It's regrettable, and I wouldn't have done what I did\nhad I known the mask concealed such beauty.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Hri_m01_003: Rather, I would have taken a more gentlemanly\napproach.
MID_LGA_1_M08_Hri_m01: <BLN>I regret it.
MID_LGV_1_M08_Miw_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_Miw_m01_001: Please! Beware of that paradise...
MID_LGV_1_M08_Miw_m01_002: No one, not one single person, has ever returned!
MID_LGA_1_M08_Miw_m01: <BLN>Be careful...
MID_LGV_1_M08_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B01_m01_001: Remember how in last month's qualifiers, the\nintroductory spiel mentioned the warlike Lydia?
MID_LGV_1_M08_B01_m01_002: Well, I've got some Lydia blood in me. Descendants\nof those old peoples are all over the place today.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B01_m01_003: The distant past becomes a lot more interesting when\nyou discover a personal connection to it.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B01_m01: <BLN>Not to brag, but...
MID_LGV_1_M08_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B02_m01_001: We're coming up on half a year since the start of the\nHeroic Games, and every match is still amazing!
MID_LGV_1_M08_B02_m01_002: If the qualifiers were that good, I can only dream of\nwhat the finals have in store for us.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B02_m01: <BLN>I never get tired of it.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B03_m01_001: Folks whose bets pay out tend to loosen their purse\nstrings. They've been tossing me plenty of coin.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B03_m01_002: When they lose, though, they take it out on me.\nYou have to choose carefully who to beg from.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B03_m01: <BLN>Which type are you?
MID_LGV_1_M08_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B04_m01_001: Do you know about panteres? They're a kind of sleek,\nblack feline found in the west.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B04_m01_002: A certain knight of Arago is nicknamed for them.\nThey're a truly fearsome breed of animal.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B04_m01: <BLN>Do you know about panteres?
MID_LGV_1_M08_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B05_m01_001: Hey, have you ever heard the old stories about the\nhuge bulls?
MID_LGV_1_M08_B05_m01_002: They're called catoblepae! They'd stand and fight no\nmatter what they faced!
MID_LGA_1_M08_B05_m01: <BLN>Have you heard about this one?
MID_LGV_1_M08_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B06_m01_001: Smyrnos's beloved cats require an awful lot of fish.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B06_m01_002: He prizes freshness above all else, so I find it easier\nto go fishing than hunt for a seller.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B06_m01_003: Thanks to that, I'm as good a fisher as any\nprofessional angler out there. How is this my life?
MID_LGA_1_M08_B06_m01: <BLN>I'm supposed to be a priest...
MID_LGV_1_M08_B07_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B07_m01_001: I'd love it if I could secure a verbal agreement with\nthe Divine Sovereign to become a court merchant.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B07_m01_002: But I already know the direct approach won't get\nme anywhere.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B07_m01_003: Maybe it'd be faster to try that red-headed priest.\nThey say she's often seen at his side.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B07_m01: <BLN>What was her name again?
MID_LGV_1_M08_B08_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B08_m01_001: My child will be born soon, so I'm trying to be more\ndevout than usual.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B08_m01_002: Should I ask for Mars's blessing for a strong child?\nOr Credna's blessing for a clever one?
MID_LGA_1_M08_B08_m01: <BLN>Who should I pray to?
MID_LGV_1_M08_B09_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B09_m01_001: Some people like bards, but for me, it's all about the\nstreet performers!
MID_LGV_1_M08_B09_m01_002: They do it all! If it's just a song with nothing else,\nI always fall asleep.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B09_m01: <BLN>I know what I like...
MID_LGV_1_M08_B10_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B10_m01_001: I get the feeling lately with some people that they're\non more than booze.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B10_m01_002: Their hollow eyes and half smiles, and the way they\ndrool...even the strongest ale won't do that to you.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B10_m01: <BLN>What could it be?
MID_LGV_1_M08_B11_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B11_m01_001: Yet another thief?! And this time they stole a whole\nshelf of stuff?! Come on!
MID_LGV_1_M08_B11_m01_002: If one more robbery of this scale happens on my\nwatch, they're gonna start docking my pay.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B11_m01: <BLN>You've gotta be kidding!
MID_LGV_1_M08_B12_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B12_m01_001: My apprentice is about to welcome a kid to the\nfamily. Maybe it's time he founded his own shop.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B12_m01_002: I've taught him what I can, and his skills are at least\ngood enough to support a child.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B12_m01: <BLN>He's come a long way.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B13_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B13_m01_001: Where's my dad? He said he'd bring me back a\nsouvenir from his voyage.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B13_m01_002: Maybe he couldn't afford one after losing all his\nmoney gambling again.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B13_m01: <BLN>Dad, where are you?
MID_LGV_1_M08_B14_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B14_m01_001: Children say the strangest things. I thought he\nwanted to be a sailor when he grew up.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B14_m01_002: But then he said, "I don't want to be a sailor! I want\nto be a boat!" What in the world does that mean?
MID_LGA_1_M08_B14_m01: <BLN>What a strange kid.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B15_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B15_m01_001: The flavor of dates changes depending on how dry\nthey are. I like them a little moist.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B15_m01_002: But my sweetheart likes them bone dry. It can be\nfrustrating when your tastes don't match like that.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B15_m01: <BLN>People like what they like, but...
MID_LGV_1_M08_B16_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B16_m01_001: Prepare yourselves, citizens of the capital! The stars\nbegin to quake! The end is nigh!
MID_LGV_1_M08_B16_m01_002: Remember the prophesies of Jehoshaphat!\nThe Herald of the Pale Raven's arrival is at hand!
MID_LGA_1_M08_B16_m01: <BLN>Hear me, citizens!
MID_LGV_1_M08_B17_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B17_m01_001: Thermae are wonderful. The water is refreshing, and\nyou meet all kinds of people as you bathe.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B17_m01_002: Even food and drink taste better after a long soak.\nI can't recommend it enough.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B17_m01_003: The only thing is to be careful you don't fall asleep.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B17_m01: <BLN>Thermae are wonderful.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B18_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B18_m01_001: I've had it up to here with that noblewoman.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B18_m01_002: I bent over backwards to get silk from Sai, but all she\nsays is "the texture is off" or "I don't like the color."
MID_LGV_1_M08_B18_m01_003: I try and I try, but I just can't win with those\ndignitaries in the guesthouses.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B18_m01: <BLN>I've had it up to here with her...
MID_LGV_1_M08_B19_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B19_m01_001: I go to the theater every single day to see the face of\nmy favorite actor.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B19_m01_002: He makes me so happy...but it is a drain on\nmy finances.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B19_m01: <BLN>He makes me so happy...
MID_LGV_1_M08_B20_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B20_m01_001: Aurora's mother, Yu Phas, is the daughter of the\ndemon god Balor.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B20_m01_002: I'd bet that Balor dragged the folk who went missing\ninto the underworld.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B20_m01_003: It's a horrific thought, but I can't see any other\nexplanation.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B20_m01: <BLN>It's horrific...
MID_LGV_1_M08_B21_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B21_m01_001: Saraminians and folks like the Har Hali are\ncollectively known as the forest peoples.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B21_m01_002: All of them trace their lineage back to the old\nkingdom of Damascar.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B21_m01_003: They're also world-class shipbuilders. The ancestors\nthey have in common must have been seafarers.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B21_m01: <BLN>Speaking of the forest peoples...
MID_LGV_1_M08_B22_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B22_m01_001: Most of what we know about Pallraven comes from\nthe poems left by the prophet Jehoshaphat.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B22_m01_002: When the world is in turmoil and in need of a savior,\nthe old god promised to send a white raven.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B22_m01_003: It will signal the turning of the tide to salvation.\nThat's the short version, at any rate.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B22_m01: <BLN>The legend of Pallraven...
MID_LGV_1_M08_B23_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B23_m01_001: Flamma is a double-edged sword. To be sure,\nit grants a tremendous amount of power.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B23_m01_002: But decent folk should have no need for it, no matter\ntheir circumstances.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B23_m01: <BLN>I wouldn't touch the stuff.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B24_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B24_m01_001: I heard from the sailors that there's a ship graveyard\nout in the Danann Sea.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B24_m01_002: Missing ships that were presumed sunk amass there\nand float aimlessly.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B24_m01_003: And if you stumble into it, you'll become trapped in\nthat mass, never to return...
MID_LGV_1_M08_B24_m01_004: Goddess, what a horrible fate! Saint Seiros,\nprotect me!
MID_LGA_1_M08_B24_m01: <BLN>Have you heard this ghastly story?
MID_LGV_1_M08_B25_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B25_m01_001: I turned up something curious while researching\nthe Flame Lords.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B25_m01_002: It appears that there was one Flame Lord who\nwas awarded the title of Blackfire.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B25_m01_003: But for some reason, no record of this individual\nremains in the temples at Dagsion.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B25_m01_004: I wonder if they became a problem and their\nexistence was intentionally scrubbed.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B25_m01: <BLN>Here's a curious finding...
MID_LGV_1_M08_B26_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B26_m01_001: Even amongst the priests, only a select few are\npermitted to meet with Aurora.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B26_m01_002: For that reason, many among those who work in this\ntemple do not believe that Aurora even exists.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B26_m01_003: It's a miserable state of affairs, but there's not much\nwe can do about it.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B26_m01: <BLN>What can we do?
MID_LGV_1_M08_B27_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B27_m01_001: The throne of Brezarant has been vacant for some\ntime now.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B27_m01_002: They're trying to find a successor, but so far they\nhaven't come up with any suitable candidates.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B27_m01_003: Their past is littered with bloody feuds between\nmembers of the royal line.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B27_m01_004: The Zodiac Incident is an especially famous example.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B27_m01_005: The thirteen children of the king vied for the throne\nin a vicious struggle against each other.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B27_m01_006: To avoid further such incidents, they choose their\nsuccessors with great care these days.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B27_m01: <BLN>The throne of Brezarant...
MID_LGV_1_M08_B28_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B28_m01_001: A bloodmark is a sign of divine power within.\nIt is passed down through family lines.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B28_m01_002: If you meet anyone who has a bloodmark, you know\nthere's a god somewhere in their family tree.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B28_m01: <BLN>What's a bloodmark, you ask?
MID_LGV_1_M08_B29_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B29_m01_001: Famous among the demigods is the hero Arago,\nwho founded the eponymous kingdom.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B29_m01_002: Also, the champion Breza, whose land of Brezarant\nwas recognized after a bout against Hanno of Arago.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B29_m01_003: There is also Vandahl, the Swashbuckler King, who\nfounded the greatest merchant house in Dagda.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B29_m01_004: And of course, I need say no more of the legendary\nbard Cohen.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B29_m01: <BLN>The most well-known demigods...
MID_LGV_1_M08_B30_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B30_m01_001: I told you not to come around here again.
MID_LGA_1_M08_B30_m01: <BLN>Get out of my sight.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B31_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M08_B31_m01_001: I've only been to Dagda's temple once, but I nearly\nkeeled over from climbing all those stairs.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B31_m01_002: My love couldn't endure it and went home before\nwe reached the top.
MID_LGV_1_M08_B31_m01_003: Surely the gods have a better way than trudging up\nand down those steps on their own feet!
MID_LGA_1_M08_B31_m01: <BLN>I thought I was going to die.